[h1]ZP_Research[/h1]
A server-side research framework for DayZ that turns scavenged loot into research points and spends them on a faction technology tree. The mod ships no content: every chain, point type, faction and tree node is admin-defined JSON. Built for the [UA] STALKER: Zone Protocol server; the tree and its balance are yours to define.

[b]What it does[/b]
[list]
[*]Processing stations: static in-world devices with cargo. Put raw materials in; the station runs a timed cycle in the background (it survives server restarts) and produces a sample or a finished data blank.
[*]Samples, blanks and carriers: a sample carries hidden fields (content, purity) read by machines; a data blank is an ordinary item whose name tells the player what it is; a carrier keeps its point type and amount hidden until it is identified at a terminal.
[*]Purity: a base roll times input quality plus module bonuses; the next station multiplies its output chance by it.
[*]Points and the tree: blanks and carriers are deposited at a faction terminal; points live in a faction pool; tree nodes cost points and optionally items, research is instant or a timed project, and nodes gate processing rules, so the tree really unlocks production.
[*]Faction isolation: factions are recognised by armband; terminals and devices belong to factions, and nobody reads another faction's tree or uses its stations.
[*]Admin surface: all configuration is JSON under the server profile, hot-reloadable with !zp reload, editable in game with !zp editor, and with a self-contained WYSIWYG web editor (one HTML file) that draws chains and the tree as graphs and mirrors the server's own validation before you restart.
[*]Three ready-made content packs in the repository: a minimal loop, the author's test stand, and the full Zone Protocol set (7 factions, 7 trees, 1087 rules).
[/list]
[b]Requires[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1559212036]Community Framework[/url].
[b]Companion[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3802267228]ZP_Research_VPP[/url], the optional VPP Admin Tools tab with the admin permission gate.
[b]Source code[/b] [url=https://github.com/covalschi/ZP_Research]github.com/covalschi/ZP_Research[/url]

[b]Licence[/b]
Repacking into your own server pack is allowed. Licence: MIT (see LICENSE and NOTICE in the repository).

